      "writtenOn": "2023-06-01T16:58:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see why. Assume a type where `sizeof(T) \u003d\u003d 8` and `alignof(T) \u003d\u003d 4` (eg, `double` with only 4-byte alignment). That should be fine, right? The storage in the class will be aligned to 8 bytes, and the stack allocated ones in the constructor will be (possibly) 4 byte aligned, but still tightly packed. The `memcpy` should work in that case, right?",
      "parentUuid": "240cd92d_35e43fbd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 42
      },
